# Files agents should never read or index. Keeps a stray search from pulling
# hundreds of megabytes of dependencies or generated output into context.
#
# This is about attention, not secrecy — `.gitignore` still governs what gets
# committed. Anything genuinely secret is listed here as well as there.

# Dependencies — 936MB, never useful to read
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Build output and caches
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
apps/web/dist/
.wrangler/
.maestro-debug/
.metro-health-check*

# Generated native projects — regenerated by prebuild, never hand-edited.
# Anchored: bare `android/` also matches store/metadata/android/, which agents
# do need for listing copy.
/android/
/ios/
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/

# Secrets and signing material — agents have no reason to open these
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
*service-account*.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
credentials.json

# Large binaries with no readable content. Images are deliberately NOT listed:
# hiding them would also hide their existence from the brand, icon, and
# screenshot workflows, and an agent only pays for an image if asked to open one.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.ttf
*.otf
*.woff
*.woff2

# Noise
.DS_Store
*.orig.*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
